comment.narrative:
KFW phase IV.1: 
- Finalize the EIA for the above-mentioned Hill Lakes in Qaa and Kefraya (Bekaa region); and construction of Irrigation networks in those sites;
- Create and produce an Infographics Video to showcase the achievements undertaken under this phase.

KFW phase IV.2: 
- Construction of irrigation canals and networks using labor-intensive approach in 8 sites: Qobbet Chamra, Bakhoun-Beqaasefrine, (North Lebanon), Anjar, Chmistar, Qaa, Haouch el Refka, Qab Elias and West Baalbeck Main Canal (Bekaa Region). Other potential sites: Hermel, Zahlé, Deir el Ahmar and Jdita;
- Prepare and submit the EIA for Zgharta- Ehden and Mishmish Hill Lakes (North Lebanon), and Construction of Irrigation Network and Hill lake using labor-intensive approach in those sites;
- Design of Irrigation Canals and Hill Lakes for Al Qaa, Haouch el Refka, Qab Elias, Hermel, Zahlé, Jdita, Qobbet Chamra, Bakhoun-Beqaasefrine, Zgharta- Ehden and Mishmish;
- Implement Capacity Building sessions for farmers and laborers.

KFW phase IV.4:
- Elaboration of selection criteria and identification of beneficiaries to initiate the implementation of Rainwater Harvesting Systems using labor-intensive approach with the ACTED (implementing partner).
- Identification of new sites to implement irrigation canals and hill lakes
- Identification of action with regards to solid waste as aftermath of Beirut Port Explosion, pending the identification of sites for landfill by the government.
